\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Acquisition witness}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{An \strong{acquisition witness} is a prespecified evaluation showing that a
trained policy succeeds on an independently checked strategy family, transfer
family, or effective-support region that the base evaluation procedure did not
reach at the same inference budget.}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal motivated by the elicitation-versus-acquisition
debate in \citef{liu2025understanding} and \citef{yue2025does}. The witness
must specify its threshold, sampling procedure, and independence conditions.
An appealing trace selected after observing the trained model is insufficient.}

\p{A witness is finite evidence, not proof of exact support expansion. It
strengthens a gain claim by testing a declared alternative explanation.}
